  {
   "id": 25,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1020,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 24,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 9 - Long-form continuation with reference and mask controls (edit a long plate)\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE (+ Fun ControlNet Union for the optional pose control).\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: a long plate, its mask video (same length and size), <Picture 1>; optionally a long pose render. Set Reference to Video's width / height to the plate's size.\n\n**Controls**: queue the graph once per segment (or set the Run batch count): each run continues where the last accepted segment ended; overlap_frames 39 (exact sound boundary) / 22 / 56; approval = accept unless drift / accept / always ask; a held segment waits in pending/ until `decision` on Next accepts or rejects it; restart archives the session. Next cuts the plate, mask and pose video to each segment (only that segment is decoded); sound = keep the source video's sound (needs exactly 24 fps) / generate / regenerate where masked; Image Composite Masked puts the generated pixels over the plate only inside the mask (exact elsewhere). Enable the two `optional` nodes for pose control.\n\n**Output**: each run saves the segment's NEW frames as an MP4 preview; the whole film is output/h3_continuation/<session>/frames (numbered 16-bit PNG, any sequence loader / editor) + audio/ (one WAV per segment, back to back). The session ends at the plate's last frame.\n\n**Limits**: no Subject Crop inside a long run (it would have to sit between the cut and the encode): for a high-resolution crop, crop the whole plate first (workflow 7's crop + save), run this on the crop, uncrop after. The plate must be on the 16 px grid.\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# 9 - Long-form continuation with reference and mask controls (edit a long plate)\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE (+ Fun ControlNet Union for the optional pose control).\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: a long plate, its mask video (same length and size), <Picture 1>; optionally a long pose render. Set Reference to Video's width / height to the plate's size.\n\n**Controls**: queue the graph once per segment (or set the Run batch count): each run continues where the last accepted segment ended; overlap_frames 39 (exact sound boundary) / 22 / 56; approval = accept unless drift / accept / always ask; a held segment waits in pending/ until `decision` on Next accepts or rejects it; restart archives the session. Next cuts the plate, mask and pose video to each segment (only that segment is decoded); sound = keep the source video's sound (needs exactly 24 fps) / generate / regenerate where masked; Image Composite Masked puts the generated pixels over the plate only inside the mask (exact elsewhere). Enable the two `optional` nodes for pose control.\n\n**Output**: each run saves the segment's NEW frames as an MP4 preview; the whole film is output/h3_continuation/<session>/frames (numbered 16-bit PNG, any sequence loader / editor) + audio/ (one WAV per segment, back to back). The session ends at the plate's last frame.\n\n**Limits**: no Subject Crop inside a long run (it would have to sit between the cut and the encode): for a high-resolution crop, crop the whole plate first (workflow 7's crop + save), run this on the crop, uncrop after. The plate must be on the 16 px grid.\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
